 "text": "Hello! How' everything today? Congratulations! A century is a nice goal. Most rides break it in the second half if you start genuinely evenly. Roughly three to four hours if you ride at a reasonable pace. Faster riders can do it in two and a half. It is. Plan food and toilet stop every two hours or so, and remember to drink before you thirst. That's a solid plan. Doing a twenty mile ride and then splitting the difference with your home loop gives you a solid base. Three to four rides of about half that distance each with a few easy miles before and after is good schedule.",
